_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 10
---
order: 10
---
short_label: XIII.10
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an equilateral pentagon is inscribed ina circle, then the square on the side of the pentagon equals the sum of the squares on the sides of the hexagon and the decagon inscribed in the same circle.
----
proof:

Let {ABCDE|circT} be a circle, and let the equilateral pentagon {ABCDE|CDEAB} be inscribed in the circle {ABCDE|circT}.

I say that the square on the side of the pentagon {ABCDE|CDEAB} equals the sum of the squares on the side of the hexagon and on that of the decagon inscribed in the circle {ABCDE|circT}.

