    // The construction draws the radii, the two perpendiculars FH, FL and
    // the joins; the walk then lights the arcs the proof halves and doubles,
    // the angles at F, A, B, N, K, and the equiangular pairs ABF / BFN and
    // AKB / AKN, ending on II.2's sum of the two rectangles.
    //
    // Joyce's AG, FK and FM run from end to end; the proof draws AF and
    // carries it to G, draws FH and FL from F and carries them on to K and
    // M, so AF, FG, FH, HK, FL, LM are solid slide twins, hidden at rest
    // (initiallyHidden), and Joyce's three lines stay out of the slide sets.
    // Transparent targets: the sides AB, CD, the pieces AL, LK, LN, AN, BN,
    // the triangles ABF, BFN, AKB, AKN (explicit ;0 faces), the arcs, and
    // circT, a faceless twin of the filled circle that the refs light. The
    // pentagon refs go to CDEAB, Joyce's own transparent pentagon, not to
    // the filled CDEABdup. Arc helpers m* are uncoloured points on the
    // circle. Right angles at H and L are red squares.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): only C and D, free — the
    // given pentagon's base, standing from slide 1. Every other point is
    // derived and listed per slide; nothing to defer.
