            { text: "“on the sides of the hexagon and the decagon inscribed in the same circle.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["circT"] },
            { text: "Let {ABCDE|circT} be a circle,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["circT"] },
            { text: "and let the equilateral pentagon {ABCDE|CDEAB} be inscribed in the circle {ABCDE|circT}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["CDEAB"] },
            { text: "I say that the square on the side of the pentagon {ABCDE|CDEAB} equals the sum of the squares",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "on the side of the hexagon and on that of the decagon inscribed in the circle {ABCDE|circT}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["circT"] },
            { text: "Take the center {F} of the circle,",
              visible: CEN,
              highlighted: ["F"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "F", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "III.1" }] },
            { text: "join {AF} and carry it through to the point {G}, and join {FB}.",
              visible: J1,
              highlighted: ["AF","FG","G","BF"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "FG", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "G",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "BF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }, { ref: "I.Post.2" }] },
            { text: "Draw {FH} from {F} perpendicular to {AB}",
              visible: P1,
              highlighted: ["FH","AB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "FH",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "H",   name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "rtH", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.12" }] },
            { text: "and carry it through to {K},",
              visible: P2,
              highlighted: ["HK","K"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "HK", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "K",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.2" }] },
            { text: "join {AK} and {KB},",
              visible: P3,
              highlighted: ["AK","BK"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AK", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "BK", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "draw {FL} from {F} perpendicular to {AK},",
              visible: P4,
              highlighted: ["FL","AK"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "FL",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "L",   name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "rtL", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.12" }] },
            { text: "carry it through to {M}, and join {KN}.",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["LM","M","KN","N"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "LM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "M",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "N",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "KN", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.2" }, { ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Since the circumference {ABCG|arcABCG} equals the circumference {AEDG|arcAEDG},",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["arcABCG","arcAEDG"] },
            { text: "and in them {ABC|arcABC} equals {AED|arcAED},",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["arcABC","arcAED"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder, the circumference {CG|arcCG}, equals the remainder {GD|arcGD}.",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["arcCG","arcGD"] },
            { text: "But {CD|arcCD} belongs to a pentagon, therefore {CG|arcCG} belongs to a decagon.",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["arcCD","arcCG"] },
            { text: "And, since {FA} equals {FB}, and {FH} is perpendicular,",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["AF","BF","FH","rtH"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {AFK} equals the angle {KFB}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["angAFK","angKFB"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angAFK", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angKFB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.5" }, { ref: "I.26" }] },
            { text: "Hence the circumference {AK|arcAK} equals {KB|arcKB}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcAK","arcKB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "III.26" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the circumference {AB|arcAB} is double the circumference {BK|arcKB}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcAB","arcKB"] },
            { text: "Therefore the straight line {AK} is a side of a decagon.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["AK"] },
            { text: "For the same reason {AK|arcAK} is double {KM|arcKM}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcAK","arcKM","rtL"] },
            { text: "Now, since the circumference {AB|arcAB} is double the circumference {BK|arcKB},",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcAB","arcKB"] },
            { text: "while the circumference {CD|arcCD} equals the circumference {AB|arcAB},",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcCD","arcAB"] },
            { text: "therefore the circumference {CD|arcCD} is also double the circumference {BK|arcKB}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcCD","arcKB"] },
            { text: "But the circumference {CD|arcCD} is also double {CG|arcCG},",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcCD","arcCG"] },
            { text: "therefore the circumference {CG|arcCG} equals the circumference {BK|arcKB}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcCG","arcKB"] },
            { text: "But {BK|arcKB} is double {KM|arcKM}, since {KA|arcAK} is so also,",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcKB","arcKM","arcAK"] },
            { text: "therefore {CG|arcCG} is also double {KM|arcKM}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcCG","arcKM"] },
            { text: "But, further, the circumference {CB|arcCB} is also double the circumference {BK|arcKB},",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcCB","arcKB"] },
            { text: "for the circumference {CB|arcCB} equals {BA|arcAB}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcCB","arcAB"] },
            { text: "Therefore the whole circumference {GB|arcGB} is also double {BM|arcBM}.",
              visible: X1,
              highlighted: ["arcGB","arcBM"] },
            { text: "Hence the angle {GFB} is double the angle {BFM}.",
              visible: X2,
              highlighted: ["angGFB","angBFM"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angGFB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angBFM", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.33" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {GFB} is double the angle {FAB},",
              visible: X3,
              highlighted: ["angGFB","angFAB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angFAB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "for the angle {FAB} equals the angle {ABF|angABF}.",
              visible: X3,
              highlighted: ["angFAB","angABF"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angABF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore the angle {BFN|angBFM} equals the angle {FAB}.",
              visible: X3,
              highlighted: ["angBFM","angFAB"] },
            { text: "But the angle {ABF|angABF} is common to the two triangles {ABF} and {BFN},",
              visible: X3,
              highlighted: ["angABF","ABF","BFN"] },
            { text: "therefore the remaining angle {AFB} equals the remaining angle {BNF}.",
              visible: X4,
              highlighted: ["angAFB","angBNF"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angAFB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angBNF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the triangle {ABF} is equiangular with the triangle {BFN}.",
              visible: X4,
              highlighted: ["ABF","BFN"] },
            { text: "Therefore, proportionally the straight line {AB} is to {BF} as {FB} is to {BN}.",
              visible: X4,
              highlighted: ["AB","BF","BN"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.4" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectangle {AB} by {BN} equals the square on {BF}.",
              visible: X4,
              highlighted: ["AB","BN","BF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.17" }] },
            { text: "Again, since {AL} equals {LK}, while {LN} is common and at right angles,",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["AL","LK","LN","rtL"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {KN} equals the base {AN}.",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["KN","AN"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.4" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the angle {LKN} also equals the angle {LAN}.",
              visible: Y1,
              highlighted: ["angLKN","angLAN"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angLKN", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angLAN", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.4" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {LAN} equals the angle {KBN},",
              visible: Y2,
              highlighted: ["angLAN","angKBN"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angKBN", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the angle {LKN} also equals the angle {KBN}.",
              visible: Y2,
              highlighted: ["angLKN","angKBN"] },
            { text: "And the angle at {A|angLAN} is common to the two triangles {AKB} and {AKN}.",
              visible: Y2,
              highlighted: ["angLAN","AKB","AKN"] },
            { text: "Therefore the remaining angle {AKB|angAKB} equals the remaining angle {KNA|angKNA}.",
              visible: Y3,
              highlighted: ["angAKB","angKNA"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angAKB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angKNA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the triangle {KBA} is equiangular with the triangle {KNA}.",
              visible: Y3,
              highlighted: ["AKB","AKN"] },
            { text: "Therefore, proportionally the straight line {BA} is to {AK} as {KA} is to {AN}.",
              visible: Y3,
              highlighted: ["AB","AK","AN"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectangle {BA} by {AN} equals the square on {AK}.",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["AB","AN","AK"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.17" }] },
            { text: "But the rectangle {AB} by {BN} was also proved equal to the square on {BF},",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["AB","BN","BF"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the rectangle {AB} by {BN} and the rectangle {BA} by {AN},",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["AB","BN","AN"] },
            { text: "that is, the square on {BA}, equals the sum of the squares on {BF} and {AK}.",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["AB","BF","AK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "rectangle AB by BN + rectangle BA by AN = square on AB", ref: "II.2" }] },
            { text: "And {BA} is a side of the pentagon, {BF} of the hexagon, and {AK} of the decagon.",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["AB","BF","AK"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "IV.15.Cor" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, if an equilateral pentagon is inscribed in a circle,",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["CDEAB","circT"] },
            { text: "then the square on the side of the pentagon equals the sum of the squares",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "on the sides of the hexagon and the decagon inscribed in the same circle.",
              visible: CONS,
              highlighted: ["BF","AK"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
